1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
A rainbow is not hanging in one place in the sky.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
It appears only when the Sun is behind you and water droplets are ahead.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Inside each raindrop, sunlight bends as it enters the water.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
That bend spreads white light into many colours.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Inside the drop, light reflects, then bends again as it leaves.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Only certain rays from certain droplets reach your eyes at the right angle.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Move a little, and a different set of droplets sends colour to you.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
The rainbow is actually a circle; from the ground, the Earth hides most of it.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,000
So a rainbow is a meeting of sunlight, water, and your exact point of view.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,000
That is why no one else sees precisely the same rainbow that you do.
